WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:07.425
This page lists every legal mechanism, oversight body, and crisis resource available to Canadians seeking accountability.

00:00:07.375 --> 00:00:08.965
Military.

00:00:08.965 --> 00:00:10.352
Federal.

00:00:10.352 --> 00:00:11.988
International.

00:00:11.988 --> 00:00:13.295
Legal.

00:00:13.295 --> 00:00:14.704
Media.

00:00:14.704 --> 00:00:16.454
Crisis support.

00:00:16.454 --> 00:00:18.329
All in one place.

00:00:18.329 --> 00:00:24.840
Military complaints: the Military Police Complaints Commission — one year filing window, no lawyer required.

00:00:24.840 --> 00:00:29.386
The DND and CF Ombudsman — independent from the chain of command.

00:00:29.386 --> 00:00:32.193
CFNIS complaints can be filed directly.

00:00:32.193 --> 00:00:36.340
Federal oversight: NSICOP reviews national security matters.

00:00:36.340 --> 00:00:39.124
NSIRA provides intelligence review.

00:00:39.124 --> 00:00:43.181
The Foreign Interference Commission is a special investigative body.

00:00:43.181 --> 00:00:50.829
The Public Sector Integrity Commissioner handles whistleblower complaints — though in eighteen years, only seven cases were referred to tribunal.

00:00:50.829 --> 00:00:57.909
International mechanisms: the United Nations Special Rapporteur on Disability has already raised concerns about MAID.

00:00:57.909 --> 00:01:03.340
The International Criminal Court has jurisdiction — Canada is a Rome Statute signatory.

00:01:03.340 --> 00:01:08.261
The Magnitsky Act enables sanctions against officials who commit human rights abuses.

00:01:08.261 --> 00:01:10.011
Crisis support.

00:01:10.011 --> 00:01:17.999
Veterans Affairs Crisis Line: 1-800-268-7708 — twenty-four hours a day, seven days a week.

00:01:17.999 --> 00:01:21.420
Canada Suicide Prevention: 9-8-8.

00:01:21.420 --> 00:01:26.874
Crisis Services Canada: 1-833-456-4566.

00:01:26.874 --> 00:01:28.681
You are not alone.
